The seasons theme's faces (~/.config/themes/seasons/).

Alegreya Sans comes from Google Fonts' repository, which carries the
upstream project's released TTFs together with its licence:
    https://github.com/google/fonts   (branch main)
It is under the SIL Open Font License 1.1 (OFL-1.1): free to use, bundle
and redistribute, not to sell on its own; the licence text travels with the
files (OFL-AlegreyaSans.txt here). No file was modified.

Alegreya Sans -- the UI face (theme.conf font=): the bar, the toolbox, the
    popup panels, the launcher, wofi, mako, mpv's OSD and subtitles, the LLM
    chat's headings, Nautilus's document face.
    By Juan Pablo del Peral (Huerta Tipografica;
    https://github.com/huertatipografica/Alegreya-Sans), version 2.004.
    A humanist sans with a calligraphic, hand-drawn rhythm: warm and organic,
    which suits a theme about nature and the calendar, and very readable at
    11-13 px. True small caps ("smcp", "c2sc") for the almanac-style labels
    and running heads, "tnum" and "lnum" for readouts (the base stylesheets
    ask for tnum; lnum stops the old-style figures bobbing in the clock).
    Static weights, so every weight the stylesheets ask for is a real cut:
    Regular 400, Medium 500, Bold 700, and Italic. No SemiBold: where the
    base asks for 600 the theme asks for 500 or 700 explicitly.
    GSUB (probed 2026-10-24): aalt c2sc case ccmp dnom frac liga lnum locl
    numr onum ordn pnum sinf smcp ss01-ss05 subs sups tnum.
    Coverage: 2109 glyphs, Latin with Latin Extended; it has the middle dot
    and the ellipsis, but none of the symbols U+25B8 U+25CF U+2600 U+2744
    U+266A U+2387 U+273F U+2713 -- fontconfig falls back per glyph to IBM
    Plex Sans (theme.conf font= lists it second) or Noto, and Font Awesome
    is the icon fallback as everywhere.
    Metrics: 1000 units per em, hhea ascent 900 / descent -300 / gap 0, a
    1.20 em line (IBM Plex Sans: 1.30) and narrower letters than Plex -- so
    most panels come out a little smaller than cyberpunk's
    (~/.config/themes/seasons/panel.css's header has the sizes).
    Files:  AlegreyaSans-Regular.ttf  AlegreyaSans-Medium.ttf
            AlegreyaSans-Bold.ttf     AlegreyaSans-Italic.ttf
    Source: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/google/fonts/main/ofl/alegreyasans/<file>
            licence: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/google/fonts/main/ofl/alegreyasans/OFL.txt
                     (saved as OFL-AlegreyaSans.txt)
    (The directory also has Thin through Black with italics; only these
    four are used, so only these four are here.)

Source Code Pro -- the readout and terminal face (term.font=, font_mono=):
    COSMIC Terminal, kitty, the bar's mono readouts, code in the LLM chat,
    Nautilus's monospace.
    By Paul D. Hunt (Adobe; https://github.com/adobe-fonts/source-code-pro),
    OFL-1.1. A humanist mono, so it pairs naturally with Alegreya Sans, and
    it has the Bold COSMIC Terminal needs (theme.py check verifies it).
    NOT copied here: it is Fedora's adobe-source-code-pro-fonts package
    (/usr/share/fonts/adobe-source-code-pro-fonts/), installed with the
    system. No other theme uses it for the terminal yet (orbit: JetBrains
    Mono, lofi: Rec Mono Casual).

